# E20-S01. A .semgrepignore REPLACES Semgrep's built-in defaults (it does not extend them), so node_modules, dist and
# build are listed again next to the output and tool directories of .gitignore. Co-located *.test.ts files are source
# and are scanned like any other file: nothing here ignores a test.
#
# Everything except node_modules is anchored to the repository root with a leading slash: a source directory that is
# merely called coverage, reports, build or rules (src/server/domain/coverage/, say) must never drop out of the scan.
node_modules/
/dist/
/build/
/coverage/
/reports/
/.yarn/
/.stryker-tmp/
/.vitest/
/playwright-report/
/test-results/
# The offline copy of the Semgrep rule sets (yarn semgrep:rules): scanned with, never scanned.
/rules/
